# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A reader tells the framing from what it frames"

# TextMate's question, asked of the dialect: "would I want these two elements styled differently?"
#
# The sharktooth opens a sigil in the house's namespace. The carrier mark opens the framing that
# carries the meme, and what it names IS a control character — STX, ETX, EOT. A reader scanning a
# meme wants the framing to stand off from what the framing carries. Measured across 65 bundled
# themes the two read apart in 56 of them; carrying one keyword family between them, they read
# apart in none.

! The sharktooth opens a sigil in the house namespace

<<~ ahu #section >>
# ^ keyword.control.sharktooth.memetic-wikitext
# ^ - constant.character.carrier.stx.memetic-wikitext
#   ^^^ meta.sigil.memetic-wikitext entity.name.function.sigil.memetic-wikitext

! The carrier mark opens the framing that carries the meme

<<^ code="&#x0002;" >>
# ^ constant.character.carrier.stx.memetic-wikitext
# ^ - keyword.control.sharktooth.memetic-wikitext
#   ^^^^ meta.carrier.control.stx.memetic-wikitext entity.other.attribute-name.memetic-wikitext
